---
import ownerImage from '../assets/owners-1.png';
import ownerImage2 from '../assets/owners-2.png';
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About The Owners"
	description="Meet the idiots who run the league"
	pubDate={new Date('August 08 2021')}
	heroImage={ownerImage}
>
	<p>
		The Terrence Clarke Memorial League is the product of a long-time local friendship.
		Running out of Neenah, Wisconsin, five friends (and one dad) teamed up to make the wackiest
		fantasy leagues possible. After a couple attempts, this dynasty league is the one that stuck.
	</p>

	<h3> Sam, Injury Hell </h3>
	<p>
		The most recent champion, Sam has one goal with his draftees: superstardom or bust. While he
		has some major misses like James Bouknight and Johnny Davis, he made some home run selections
		like Franz Wagner, Cam Boozer, and Chet Holmgren. Current star: Cade Cunningham.
	</p>

	<h3> Anthony, Big boys don't kawhi </h3>
	<p>
		The first league champion and by far the most volatile drafter. He drafts people you've never
		even heard of. Sometimes it works, like when he picked Victor Wembanyama after EVERYONE passed
		on him in 2021. Other times, he picks Gus Yalden. You truly never know. Current star: Victor Wembanyama.
	</p>

	<h3> Michael, Duren Duren </h3>
	<p>
		One time champion and runner-up of the most recent season, Michael's team has ups and downs.
		This year he said he was actively tanking before going on a run in the playoffs. His team is full of
		"tank commanders", including Josh Giddey, Jonathan Kuminga, and Ace Bailey. Current star: Jalen Duren
	</p>

	<h3> Mr. L, Pokemon Max </h3>
	<p>
		The original dynasty. With sutds like Tyrese Maxey, Trey Murphy III, Evan Mobley, and Deni Avdija,
		this team is always the favorite at the beginning of the season. Even though he's coming off a down year
		of getting 4th place, he has studs like Tyran Stokes coming up in future drafts. Current star: Anthony Edwards. 
	</p>

	<h3> Matt, Pritchard Fan Club </h3>
	<p>
		Though he got 7th place last year, this is one team you shouldn't sleep on. With Brandon Miller,
		every Pacer you can think of, and the combination of Jalens Williams and Johnson, this is a team
		that can win any given week. Current star: Tyrese Haliburton.
	</p>

	<h3> Mitchell, GG's Smoke and VORP Shop </h3>
	<p>
		The only team that hasn't won a championship, but arguably the deepest team. The combination of
		Maxime Raynaud, Jabari Smith, GG Jackson, Isaiah Stewart, and Onyeka Okongwu give him the deepest center
		rotation by far. Not to mention Current star: Alperen Sengun.
	</p>
</Layout>
